1
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:09,350
Hi, Hannah. What are you up to?

2
00:00:10,530 --> 00:00:14,160
Hey, Mike. Nothing much. I’m at home.

3
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:18,160
I’m watching some TV, but it’s not very good.

4
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:20,680
I don’t want to do my homework!

5
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:22,450
How about you?

6
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,800
I’m in town. Shopping.

7
00:00:26,590 --> 00:00:34,300
I’m looking for a new jacket. Do you like this one? It’s £20.

8
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:41,575
Erm. It’s OK. It looks a bit old-fashioned though.

9
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:43,620
Which shop are you in?

10
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:49,040
Tell me you’re not looking for clothes in that old place in Green Street.

11
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:51,880
Hah! Of course I am!

12
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:55,680
You know I always like to buy my clothes here.

13
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:58,480
But their clothes are all second-hand.

14
00:00:58,940 --> 00:01:01,330
And that means they’re old-fashioned.

15
00:01:02,010 --> 00:01:07,420
I like the clothes here – they’re really cool and they’re cheap.

16
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:10,460
I’m not rich like you, you know!

17
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:15,260
Me? Rich? You’re joking of course. Hahaha.

18
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:20,880
Go to Barker’s next to the big chemist’s in Market Street.

19
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,720
They’ve got a sale on.

20
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:27,520
They’re selling everything at 30% off the original price!

21
00:01:28,410 --> 00:01:29,990
And their stuff’s really nice.

22
00:01:30,790 --> 00:01:35,090
I’m wearing one of their T-shirts now. Only £9.99!

23
00:01:36,090 --> 00:01:41,130
Yeah, that’s cool. And 30% off? Brilliant.

24
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:45,980
OK, I’m going there now. Oh no!

25
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:50,380
Now it’s raining and I haven’t got an umbrella.

26
00:01:52,510 --> 00:01:55,930
OK, it’s not far. Five minutes and I’m there.

27
00:01:57,740 --> 00:01:58,540
Moments later.

28
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:02,926
OK, here I am in Barker’s.

29
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:08,380
The shop’s really crowded. It’s because of the sale, I guess.

30
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:13,160
Maybe my mum’s there. She’s doing some shopping at the moment.

31
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:16,200
So … anything nice?

32
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:25,508
Yeah! Look at this shirt! Only £25! I want it!

33
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:29,920
Mike, are you crazy? It’s awful.

34
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:31,750
No, it’s not.

35
00:02:32,410 --> 00:02:34,510
I love wearing bright colours.

36
00:02:35,110 --> 00:02:39,920
They make me feel happy. It’s perfect for a rainy day.

37
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:43,670
I think you’re wasting your money and my time.

38
00:02:45,050 --> 00:02:48,290
Anyway – are you looking for a jacket or a shirt?

39
00:02:49,090 --> 00:02:54,050
Oh yes, you’re right. You’re better at clothes than me.

40
00:02:54,830 --> 00:02:58,150
Come and help me. You’re not doing anything, are you?

41
00:02:58,150 --> 00:03:02,760
That sounds like a bad idea. It’s raining – remember?
